So a few people, on our much earlier Häagen Dazs Belgian Chocolate video, said it wasn't the custard base so It can't be "accurate" to how HD actually make it. So this video is a custard base version but using a different cocoa powder. The OG version is identical to Häagen Dazs version, this one is very good but not as close. 
The key to getting this ice cream PERFECT is Seven Hills Cocoa Powder by the way 😉

If you want to watch the first version, click this link: https://youtu.be/WMqQvMxHbzE


What you'll need for the Ice Cream:
250ml milk @ 1.8% fat
200ml Cream @ 49% fat
100g Sugar
40g Dextrose
2 Egg Yolks
10g Cocoa Powder @ 24% fat (I used Callebaut here)(use Seven Hills cocoa powder instead)
40g Chocolate @ 70% (could reduce to 25-30g)

Extra 70% chocolate for the add in. Freeze it ahead of time to make chopping it easier.

As you can see in the video, the cocoa powder used makes a HUGE difference. I used Seven Hills first time around and that was almost exactly the same flavour profile as Häagen Dazs so if you really want to create the same taste, use that. 

I still belive the eggless version I made before is better, much mich closer to the Häagen Dazs you buy in the stores. I WILL try this again in the future with Seven Hills cocoa powder in an eggless base and do a Side/Side comparison, is that a video you'd like to see?

